The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (!IS_ERR(ci->platdata->vbus_extcon.edev)) {
    hw_write_id_reg(ci, HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2,
                    HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN,
                    HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN);
}
```
Reason:
The original code checks if the external connector (extcon) handle for VBUS is valid before writing to the `HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2` register. If the extcon handle is invalid (i.e., there is no valid external connector), the write operation is skipped, which leads to improper controller reset functionality when using the USB role-switch API.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!IS_ERR(ci->platdata->vbus_extcon.edev) || ci->role_switch) {
    hw_write_id_reg(ci, HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2,
                    HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN,
                    HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN);
}
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the condition to include a check for `ci->role_switch`. This ensures that the write to the `HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2` register occurs even when there is no valid extcon handle, as long as role-switching is enabled. This change allows for proper controller reset functionality in scenarios where the extcon handle is absent but role-switching is active.

